{
  "raw": {
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504850/learning-designer": {
      "title": "Learning Designer",
      "description": "Learning Designer • Join a well-established and supportive team to shape exceptional learning experiences • UC Level 7, Salary Range $103,259 pa - $111,865 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time Fixed Term Opportunity Until April 2027 Job no: 504850 Work type: Professional Location: Bruce Categories: Student Support Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description About us: University of Canberra is more than a university, it’s a community committed to shaping a better world through education, research, and opportunity with a strong commitment to inclusivity and reducing inequalities. Our vibrant campus in Australia’s capital city is a hub of innovation & opportunity. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate outcomes and student support, UC values progress over perfection, inclusion over competition, and real‑world impact over prestige. If you’re looking for a career that matters, where you can belong, grow, and help shape what’s next, you’ll find your place at UC. About the opportunity: Our Learning and Teaching team is seeking a passionate and collaborative Learning Designer to work closely with academic subject matter experts and teaching staff to design, develop, and deliver engaging, high-quality learning experiences across a diverse range of courses and disciplines. The Learning Designer play a key role in creating sustainable, engaging, and evidence-based learning and assessment experiences that support student success. This is an exciting opportunity for an innovative educator and learning design professional who is passionate about student-centred learning, digital pedagogy, and the effective use of educational technologies to enhance learning outcomes. Key Responsibilities: Partner with academic staff and stakeholders to design and implement innovative learning solutions that enhance the student experience. Design high-quality learning activities, assessments, and educational resources grounded in contemporary learning design principles. Develop and publish engaging digital learning materials, including interactive online resources. Provide expert advice on learning design, digital pedagogy, and educational technologies. Support the development of inclusive, flexible, and student-centred learning experiences across a range of disciplines. Manage project timelines, identify delivery risks, and ensure successful completion of learning design projects. Collaborate effectively with colleagues across the University to achieve strategic learning and teaching outcomes. About you: Demonstrated experience in learning design, instructional design, educational development, or a related field. Strong knowledge of learning design principles for online, blended, and face-to-face learning environments. Understanding and experience with H5P is highly desirable. A team player with strong written and verbal communication skills. The ability to work collaboratively across multiple projects and disciplines in a dynamic environment to meet tight deadlines Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be explored on our “ Work at UC ” site which includes: Flexible working arrangements Family-friendly policies On campus Gym, Medical services, Cafes, Post office, Supermarket and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. Professional Development offerings (study assistance, corporate programs and discounts) Access to Employee Assistance Program and a corporate private Health Plan (Bupa) How to apply: Please apply with your CV only, no other documentation is required at this stage. Please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. Working rights: Applicants who wish to apply for this position must have valid working rights at the time of submission. For job specific information: please contact Steve Bath, Deputy Director, Learning & Teaching, Steve.Bath@canberra.edu.au For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, 18 October 2026 Advertised: 09 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504828/community-engagement-coordinator": {
      "title": "Community Engagement Coordinator",
      "description": "Community Engagement Coordinator • Help shape a healthier, more connected UC community • UC Level 6, Salary Range $93,704 pa - $100,871 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time, Continuing Opportunity (0.8FTE arrangements may also be considered) Job no: 504828 Work type: Professional Location: Bruce Categories: Administration, Marketing and Communications Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Help shape a healthier, more connected UC community UC Level 6, Salary Range $93,704 pa - $100,871 pa plus 17% Super Full Time, Continuing Opportunity (0.8FTE arrangements may also be considered) About us: University of Canberra is more than a university, it’s a community committed to shaping a better world through education, research, and opportunity with a strong commitment to inclusivity and reducing inequalities. Our vibrant campus in Australia’s capital city is a hub of innovation & opportunity. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate outcomes and student support, UC values progress over perfection, inclusion over competition, and real‑world impact over prestige. If you’re looking for a career that matters, where you can belong, grow, and help shape what’s next, you’ll find your place at UC. About the role: The University of Canberra is seeking a creative and energetic Community Engagement Coordinator to help connect students with the support, resources, and services available through the UC Medical & Counselling Centre. This is an exciting opportunity to play a pivotal role in promoting student health and wellbeing through meaningful campaigns, engaging events, innovative digital content, and collaborative partnerships across the University. You'll champion the Centre's services by engaging students, promoting wellbeing initiatives, and fostering greater awareness of available health and support resources. Key responsibilities include: Developing, coordinating and delivering health promotion campaigns, wellbeing initiatives, and community engagement activities. Planning and facilitating health-themed events and activities. Building and maintaining strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders. Collaborating in the development of innovative communication and engagement strategies. Creating, coordinating and distributing engaging digital and print promotional materials. Managing and maintaining online communications channels. About you: You thrive on managing multiple priorities, being efficient, exploring new ideas, challenging conventional approaches, and identifying fresh opportunities to connect students with health and wellbeing services. To be successful in this role, you'll have: Experience in community engagement, health promotion, communications, marketing, events, or a related field. Exceptional written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated experience coordinating events, campaigns, or engagement activities. Ability to build strong relationships with stakeholders. Digital literacy and proficiency with the ability to create engaging content across multiple platforms. Strong organisational skills with a proactive, solutions-focused mindset. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights at the time of submission. How to apply: Please apply with you Resume only, no other documentation is required at this stage. Please ensure you take the time to align your Resume with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview or task. For job specific information: please contact Sam Smith, Assistant Practice Manager - sam.smith@canberra.edu.au For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 18 October 2026 Advertised: 07 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504623/snow-scholarship-program-coordinator": {
      "title": "Snow Scholarship Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Snow Scholarship Program Coordinator • Help shape the future of the next generation of leaders • UC Level 6, Salary Range $93,705 pa - $100,871 pa pro rata + 17% Super • 3-day Part-Time Continuing Opportunity | Flexible Hours Job no: 504623 Work type: Professional Location: Bruce Categories: Administration, Student Support Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Help shape the future of the next generation of leaders UC Level 6, Salary Range $93,705 pa - $100,871 pa pro rata + 17% Super 3-day Part-Time Continuing Opportunity | Flexible Hours About us: Snow Scholarships have been co-created by Snow Foundation and the University of Canberra. Snow Foundation believes in the power of education to change lives and open doors – helping students realise their potential and grow into confident, purposeful leaders. In partnership with the University of Canberra, The Snow Foundation committed $20 million to back students who have big dreams and just need the support to get there. University of Canberra’s vision is that “Together we work to empower, connect and share knowledge with our people, cultures and places.” UC is part of the fabric of the local community, and we aim to challenge the status quo through the pursuit of excellence in teaching, learning and research. The University of Canberra is deeply committed to reducing inequalities and making university accessible for students regardless of their background. About the opportunity: From the partnership between University of Canberra and the Snow Foundation, the Snow Scholarship is a new and transformative program, now in its first year, supporting students from diverse or Indigenous backgrounds from Canberra and regional or rural NSW who are facing barriers to higher education. The program provides support for the entire duration of their degree providing financial and pastoral care support, leadership development, First Nations experiences and education, and more. It’s about changing lives and creating impact, nurturing the next generation of leaders. This is a great opportunity to join the Snow Scholarship team as the Snow Scholarship Program Coordinator and play a meaningful role in a groundbreaking scholarship program at the University of Canberra, helping change the lives of students and supporting them to achieve their potential. Position Description: Snow Scholarship Program Coordinator.pdf Key Responsibilities: Coordinate the day-to-day administration and support delivery of the Snow Scholarship Program. Build strong, trusted relationships with scholars and key stakeholders. Provide empathetic, responsive, and high-quality support to students. Coordinate program activities, communications, events, and key milestones. Occasional out-of-hours activity may be required for key events. Identify opportunities to improve the scholar experience and strengthen program delivery. About You: You are dynamic, empathetic, and impact-driven, with a genuine passion for supporting students and helping them thrive. You bring strong experience in student support or program coordination, exceptional attention to detail, and the ability to build trusted relationships with students and stakeholders. This position is more than a job; it’s an opportunity to be part of a transformative program that changes lives. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be explored on our “ Work at UC ” site which includes: Flexible working arrangements and Family-friendly policies On campus Gym, Medical services, Cafes, Post office, Supermarket and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. Professional Development offerings (study assistance, corporate programs and discounts) Innovative work environment with a diverse and inclusive culture Access to Employee Assistance Program and a corporate private Health Plan (Bupa) University of Canberra embodies its Values of Everyone’s invites, Narragunnawali, Change the World, Dare to be Curious and Walk together which we are proud. UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via Connected – A Decadal Strategy 2023-2032 . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. What we need from you: To be considered for this position, submit your application through the “Apply Now” tab with your CV and a cover letter outlining why you are a strong fit for this position. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview or a written assessment. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position must have valid working rights at the time of submission. The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, the successful candidate will be required to have or obtain a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For job specific information: please contact Claire Toepfer, Snow Scholarship Program Manager, claire.toepfer@canberra.edu.au . For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . If you would like to request a reasonable adjustment to the selection process, please feel free to contact us. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 18 October 2026 Advertised: 05 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504802/lecturer-in-human-nutrition-dietetics": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Human Nutrition / Dietetics",
      "description": "Lecturer in Human Nutrition / Dietetics • Make a meaningful contribution to the future of nutrition and dietetics • Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,803pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super (Pro-rata) • Part-time (0.4 FTE – 15 hours per week), 2 years Fixed Term Opportunity Job no: 504802 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Nutrition and Dietetics Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Make a meaningful contribution to the future of nutrition and dietetics Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,803pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super (Pro-rata) Part-time (0.4 FTE – 15 hours per week), 2 years Fixed Term Opportunity About us: At the University of Canberra, we’re a welcoming and connected academic community shaped by the people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. Our research focuses on real-world challenges, working alongside partners to create outcomes that matter, while our teaching builds confidence and capability for the future. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, UC is a place where you can grow ideas, contribute knowledge, and make a difference. About the role: We are seeking an enthusiastic and innovative Lecturer in Human Nutrition or Dietetics to join our Discipline of Nutrition and Dietetics. This fixed-term, part-time opportunity is ideal for an early-career academic who is committed to excellence in teaching, student engagement, and the scholarship of learning and teaching. In this rewarding role, you will contribute significantly to the delivery and development of undergraduate and postgraduate nutrition and dietetics education. As an Education Focused academic, you will be committed to student-centred learning and innovative teaching practices, while actively contributing to the scholarly and collegial life of the School and Faculty. Key responsibilities: In this role, you will: Convene units, lead and contribute to teaching and curriculum development Coordinate units and develop contemporary, evidence-based learning materials. Deliver engaging lectures, tutorials, practical classes, laboratories, seminars, and workshops. Support and mentor students through consultation and academic guidance. Develop innovative teaching approaches that enhance student engagement and learning outcomes. Contribute to work-integrated learning and industry engagement activities. About you: To be successful in this role, you will bring: Demonstrated experience in designing, coordinating, and delivering university teaching programs. Experience teaching across undergraduate and/or postgraduate education, including online and blended learning environments. Excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to build effective relationships with students, colleagues, and industry partners. Strong oral and written communication skills. A commitment to student success, innovation in teaching, and continuous improvement. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and workplace health and safety principles. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: A PhD (or enrolled and working towards PhD completion) in Human Nutrition or Dietetics (Highly desirable). Registration as a Nutritionist or Accredited Practising Dietitian (APD), or eligibility to obtain APD status through Dietitians Australia. Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights at the time of submission. The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au How to apply: Please apply with you CV only, no other documentation is required at this stage. Please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. For job specific information: please contact Ekavi Geourgouropoulou - Discipline Lead in Nutrition and Dietetics - Ekavi.Georgousopoulou@canberra.edu.au For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 18 October 2026 Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504779/lecturer-in-pharmacy": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Pharmacy",
      "description": "Lecturer in Pharmacy • Be part of shaping the future of pharmacy practice and workforce development • Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa pro rata plus 17% Super • 2 x Part-time roles (0.6FTE, 22.5 hrs per week), Continuing & Fixed Term Opportunities Job no: 504779 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Pharmacy Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Be part of shaping the future of pharmacy practice and workforce development Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa pro rata plus 17% Super 2 x Part-time roles (0.6FTE, 22.5 hrs per week), Continuing & Fixed Term Opportunities About us: Connected and inclusive, the University of Canberra works alongside the diverse people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. We deliver practical, real-world learning that helps students build confidence, skills and futures that matter. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, we’re shaping a better world through innovation, equity, and practical impact. Through our Reconnected Strategy , UC is committed to our purpose and values in leading the national education & research sector, championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility . The University of Canberra welcomes applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity, and individuals from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds.” About the opportunity: Australia is entering a new era of pharmacy practice, with pharmacist prescribing rapidly becoming a core component of healthcare delivery. 80% of community pharmacists are predicted to become qualified prescribers within the next decade, which presents an exciting opportunity for academic leaders to be part of shaping the future of pharmacy practice and workforce development. The University of Canberra is seeking 2x part-time (0.6FTE, 22.5 hrs per week), Lecturers in Pharmacy to join our Pharmacy discipline, one for a continuing role and the other for a 12-month fixed term contract. As a Lecturer in Pharmacy, you will play a key role in delivering and enhancing the University's pharmacy programs across face-to-face, online and blended learning environments. You will also have the opportunity to develop your scholarly profile through learning and teaching scholarship, educational innovation, and research supervision activities. Position Description - Lecturer in Pharmacy (Level B).pdf Position Description - Lecturer in Pharmacy (Level B) - FT.pdf Key Responsibilities: In this role, you will: Deliver engaging lectures, tutorials, workshops and practical classes across various learning modes. Coordinate units and contribute to curriculum development, assessment design and student learning experiences. Design and evaluate innovative, authentic assessments that support student success. Develop and maintain productive relationships with healthcare organisations, professional bodies, industry and community stakeholders. Contribute to research supervision where appropriate, including Honours, Masters and PhD students. About you: To be successful in this role, you will bring: Contemporary experience in pharmacy practice and a strong understanding of current developments within the profession. Experience in tertiary teaching, assessment and/or curriculum development in pharmacy or a related health discipline. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to be teaching and mentoring your industry peers. Completion of, or substantial progress towards, a PhD in pharmacy or a related field (Desirable). Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. Eligibility: A postgraduate qualification in pharmacy, clinical pharmacy, pharmacy practice, pharmacology or a related discipline. Current registration as a pharmacist with AHPRA. Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights at the time of submission. How to apply: To be considered for this position, we require your CV and a cover letter explaining your interest, you would bring to the role and your preference for either continuing or fixed-term employment. We kindly ask that you take this opportunity to align your CV with the Position Description, ensuring that your skills and experience are clearly articulated in connection with the specific requirements of the role. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. For job specific information: please contact Mary Bushell - Discipline Lead in Pharmacy - Mary.Bushell@canberra.edu.au - 02 6206 3934. For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 25 October 2026 Advertised: 25 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504729/lecturer-in-health": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Health",
      "description": "Lecturer in Health • Inspiring the next generation of health professionals • Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time, Continuing Opportunity Job no: 504729 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Health Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Inspiring the next generation of health professionals Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super Full Time, Continuing Opportunity About us: The University of Canberra is a welcoming and connected academic community shaped by its people, cultures and environments in Australia’s capital. Our research focuses on real-world challenges, working alongside partners to create outcomes that matter, while our teaching builds confidence and capability for the future. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, UC is a place where you can grow ideas, contribute knowledge, and make a difference. About the role: UC’s Faculty of Health is currently recruiting for a passionate Lecturer in Health (education focused) to join us to inspire and prepare graduates in the evolving health, disability, and community sectors. This is an exciting opportunity for an early career academic who is dedicated to student success and wishes to contribute meaningfully to innovative, high-quality health education. This role, plays a key part in delivering engaging learning experiences across interdisciplinary health programs, working collaboratively with colleagues to support student achievement and academic excellence. Key responsibilities include: Preparing and delivering high-quality classes Coordinating units and contributing to course management and quality assurance activities. Designing innovative and authentic assessment tasks that enhance student learning and graduate outcomes. Providing academic guidance, mentorship, and support to students. About you: To be successful in this role, you will be a collegial, scholarly and inquisitive educator driven to create a positive impact on the health professional eco-system. Teaching a broad Health Science skilled subject, you will help define, guide and influence student’s professional direction. Other requirements include: Professional experience within health, disability, community health, allied health, or closely related sectors. Experience applying professional practice knowledge to teaching and learning environments. Demonstrated ability to design, develop, coordinate, and deliver undergraduate and postgraduate subjects. Experience teaching in a health-related discipline within a tertiary education environment. Strong interpersonal, communication, and stakeholder management skills. Evidence of scholarly activity and the ability to translate contemporary research into engaging and relevant teaching practices. A PhD in Health or a related discipline Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights in Australia with the ability to start in early 2027. A current ACT working with vulnerable people (WWVP) registration, or ability to obtain. How to apply: Please apply with you CV only, no other documentation is required at this stage. Please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. For job specific information: please contact Alison Shield - Head of School - Health Sciences - alison.shield@canberra.edu.au - 02 6201 2084. For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Friday 23 October 2026 Advertised: 22 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504731/lecturer-in-public-health": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Public Health",
      "description": "Lecturer in Public Health • Shape Public Health Education • Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time, Continuing Opportunity Job no: 504731 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Shape Public Health Education Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super Full Time, Continuing Opportunity About us: At the University of Canberra, we believe education should be built for real people. People with different stories, responsibilities and ways of getting here. We are a modern Australian university focused on equal access to education and providing a supportive community where our students feel safe to grow and thrive. We support students as whole people, help them build confidence and prepare them to use their qualification in work, community and life beyond university. Working at UC means contributing to a university that puts people first. #UCan@UC About the role: UC is seeking for an engaged and enthusiastic Lecturer in Public Health (education focused) to join our Faculty of Health teaching into the Masters program. Working collaboratively with Health Research Institute (HRI) you will incorporate our cutting-edge research expertise into the educational programs and supporting student achievement and academic excellence. This role plays a critical part in shaping and delivering engaging learning experiences and promoting public health for a better tomorrow. Key responsibilities: Preparing and delivering high-quality classes Coordinating units and contributing to course management and quality assurance activities. Designing innovative and authentic assessment tasks that enhance student learning and graduate outcomes. Providing academic guidance, mentorship, and support to students. About you: You are an inspiring educator committed to student success and advancing community health in preparing the next generation of public health professionals. To be considered for the role you will also have: Experience applying professional practice knowledge to teaching and learning environments. Demonstrated ability to design, develop, coordinate, and deliver undergraduate and postgraduate subjects. Experience teaching in a health-related discipline within a tertiary education environment. Strong interpersonal, communication, and stakeholder management skills. Evidence of scholarly activity and the ability to translate contemporary research into engaging and relevant teaching practices. A PhD in Epidemiology or Public Health, or a related discipline. Professional experience within public health sector (advantageous). Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, pharmacy, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position will require Australian working rights with the ability to start in early 2027. A current ACT working with vulnerable people (WWVP) registration, or ability to obtain. How to apply: Please apply with you CV only, no other documentation is required at this stage. Please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. For job specific information: please contact Alison Shield - Head of School - Health Sciences - alison.shield@canberra.edu.au - 02 6201 2084. For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Friday 23 October 2026 Advertised: 22 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504740/lecturer-in-social-work": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Social Work",
      "description": "Lecturer in Social Work • Combine your social work expertise with a passion for teaching and student development • Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time, Continuing Opportunity Job no: 504740 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Combine your social work expertise with a passion for teaching and student development Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super Full Time, Continuing Opportunity About us: At the University of Canberra, we’re a welcoming and connected academic community shaped by the people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. Our research focuses on real-world challenges, working alongside partners to create outcomes that matter, while our teaching builds confidence and capability for the future. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, UC is a place where you can grow ideas, contribute knowledge, and make a difference. About the role: Due to rapid growth, our Faculty of Health is seeking an enthusiastic and student-centred Lecturer in Social Work (Education Focused) to join our growing Discipline of Social Work. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to the discipline and help shape the future of social work education through cutting-edge teaching, clinical supervision, and curriculum innovation. This dynamic and expanding program delivers high-quality teaching helping establish innovative social work services. This role is central to the course delivery and supporting student success through their degree in combining academic teaching with clinical education and supervision. Key responsibilities: In this role, you will: Deliver engaging teaching across the social work curriculum. Coordinate units and contribute to course leadership activities. Lead the development and implementation of a student-led Social Work Clinic. Collaborate to develop curriculum aligned with accreditation standards and contemporary social work practice. Build and maintain strong partnerships with community, health, and human service organisations. Contribute to scholarship and research in teaching and learning, particularly in social work education. About you: We are looking for an experienced social work professional who is passionate about education and committed to developing future practitioners. To be successful, you will have: A Master of Social Work (Qualifying) or equivalent qualification. A PhD in Social Work or a related discipline, or a willingness to undertake doctoral studies would be advantageous At least five years' professional social work experience. Membership (or eligibility) with the Australian Association of Social Workers (AASW). Demonstrated experience supervising students undertaking field education placements. Previous teaching experience in higher education, social work, or the human services sector. Evidence of teaching quality, educational innovation, or professional training delivery. Experience working collaboratively with stakeholders across health, community, or human services sectors with existing networks in the Act and region The ability to contribute to online, blended, and face-to-face learning environments. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights at the time of submission. The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au How to apply: Please apply with you CV and a cover letter outlining your interest and suitability. Also, please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. For job specific information: please contact Lynne Keevers, Professor in Social Work, Lynne.Keevers@canberra.edu.au - 02 6206 8652 or 0448641162. For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Tuesday 20 October 2026 Advertised: 22 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504696/lecturer-in-occupational-therapy": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Lecturer in Occupational Therapy We are growing out team! The University of Canberra is seeking occupational therapists with a commitment to excellence in education, clinical practice and research to join our highly regarded team. Job no: 504696 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Teaching and Research, Occupational Therapy Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description We are growing out team! The University of Canberra is seeking occupational therapists with a commitment to excellence in education, clinical practice and research to join our highly regarded team. Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super Full Time or Part-time, Continuing Opportunity About us: Connected and inclusive, the University of Canberra works alongside the diverse people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. We deliver practical, real-world learning that helps students build confidence, skills and futures that matter. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, we’re shaping a better world through innovation, equity, and practical impact. Through our Reconnected Strategy , UC is committed to our purpose and values in leading the national education & research sector, championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility . The University of Canberra welcomes applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity, and individuals from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. About the opportunity: The University of Canberra is recruiting for an enthusiastic and committed academic to join our occupational therapy team as a Education Focus (EF) or Education Research (ER) lecturer. This is an exciting opportunity to make an impactful and meaningful contribution to teaching, scholarship, and research within a growing and highly regarded health discipline. As part of our collaborative academic team, this position plays a key role in delivering high-quality learning experiences across our Bachelor and Master of Occupational Therapy programs. This is a great opportunity to shape curriculum, drive teaching innovation, and develop a research profile aligned with the priorities of the Occupational Therapy discipline. Key Responsibilities: In this role, you will: Coordinate and deliver occupational therapy units. Lead innovative teaching practices. Prepare and deliver lectures, tutorials, workshops, practical classes, and seminars. Design, develop and review curriculum and learning materials. Assess student performance and provide high-quality feedback. Support student learning and supervise Honours and Higher Degree by Research (HDR) students (ER). Develop and contribute to a collaborative research program (ER). About you: To be successful, you will bring: Registration as an occupational therapist with AHPRA. Significant clinical experience as an occupational therapist. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching and student-centred learning. Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to engage diverse student cohorts. For Education Research role: PhD (or progress towards completion) An emerging or established research profile relevant to occupational therapy (for the research focused role option). Additional qualities that would be highly regarded include: Experience working with children and young people and/ or with within the disability sector Previous teaching, course coordination or supervision experience in higher education. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be explored on our “ Work at UC ” site which includes: Flexible working arrangements Family-friendly policies On campus Gym, Medical services, Cafes, Post office, Supermarket and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. Professional Development offerings (study assistance, corporate programs and discounts) Access to Employee Assistance Program and a corporate private Health Plan (Bupa) What we need from you: To be considered for this position, we require your CV and a cover letter explaining what skills and experience you would bring to the role and why you are interested in the position. How to apply: Please apply with you CV and a cover letter outlining your interest and suitability. Also, please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. Position Description - Lecturer in Occupational Therapy (EF) Position Description - Lecturer in Occupational Therapy (ER) Working rights: Applicants who wish to apply for this position must have valid working rights at the time of submission. WWVP: The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au For job specific information: please contact Claire Pearce - Discipline Lead in Occupational Therapy - Claire.Pearce@canberra.edu.au - 02 6206 8452. For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 18 October 2026 Advertised: 18 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504842/faculty-operations-officer": {
      "title": "Faculty Operations Officer",
      "description": "Faculty Operations Officer • Frontline administrative support, offering customer-focused service across the Faculty • UC Level 5, Salary Range $81,918 pa - $93,070 pa plus 17% Super (pro rata) • Part Time (0.6 FTE, 21 hours per week), Fixed Term Until Dec 2027 Job no: 504842 Work type: Professional Location: Bruce Categories: Administration Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description About us: Join University of Canberra where we walk together to foster an inclusive community. Together, we endeavour to empower, connect, and exchange knowledge with our diverse people, cultures, and environments. We stand firm and dedicated to upholding fundamental values such as inclusivity, honouring Indigenous cultures (Narragunnawali), driving positive change, nurturing curiosity, and promoting collaborative efforts. We are committed to leading the national education sector in championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility via Connected – A Decadal Strategy 2023-2032 . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. About the role: Are you a proactive, tech-savvy professional with a passion for supporting staff and students? Faculty of Business, Government and Law is seeking an administration focused professional to join our Faculty Operations team. In this role, you'll be the first point of contact for staff and stakeholder enquiries providing responsive, high-quality administrative services across the Faculty. Key Responsibilities: Be the friendly face at our reception desk, providing responsive, customer-focused support Deliver high-quality administrative and technical assistance to staff and stakeholders Support the coordination of Faculty events, meetings, and activities Assist with finance, HR and travel arrangements, ensuring accuracy and efficiency Collaborate closely with team members to maintain a positive and productive work environment Take a proactive approach to identifying and resolving issues, always keeping stakeholders in mind About you: Strong team player with excellent interpersonal skills Experience in administrative support, ideally in an educational or professional services setting Proficiency in Microsoft Office and comfort working with AI tools and platforms A stakeholder-focused mindset, with a commitment to delivering exceptional service Strong organisational skills and attention to detail Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits such as: Flexible working arrangements Family-friendly policies On campus Gym, Medical services, Cafes, Post office, Supermarket and Childcare facilities. Professional Development offerings (study assistance, corporate programs and discounts) Innovative work environment with a diverse and inclusive culture Access to Employee Assistance Program and a corporate private Health Plan (Bupa) How to apply: To be considered for this position, we require your Resume and a one-page cover letter explaining what skills you would bring to the role and how you meet the role requirements; no additional documents are necessary. Working rights: Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights at the time of submission. For job specific information: please contact Humi Togami-Fleurisson, Operations Manager, Faculty of Business, Government and Law, Humi.Togami-Fleurisson@canberra.edu.au For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 01 November 2026 Advertised: 16 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504870/senior-careers-consultant": {
      "title": "Senior Careers Consultant",
      "description": "Senior Careers Consultant • Make a meaningful impact on students’ career aspirations through your mentoring and guidance • UC Level 7, Salary Range $103,259 pa - $111,865 pa plus 17% Super (pro rata) • Part Time (0.4 FTE) Fixed Term Opportunity Until 24 Dec 2027 Job no: 504870 Work type: Professional Location: Bruce Categories: Administration, Student Support Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description About us: University of Canberra is more than a university, it’s a community committed to shaping a better world through education, research, and opportunity with a strong commitment to inclusivity and reducing inequalities. Our vibrant campus in Australia’s capital city is a hub of innovation & opportunity. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate outcomes and student support, UC values progress over perfection, inclusion over competition, and real‑world impact over prestige. If you’re looking for a career that matters, where you can belong, grow, and help shape what’s next, you’ll find your place at UC. About the opportunity: UC’s Careers & Employability team is seeking an experienced and passionate Senior Careers Consultant to join the Careers & Employability team. Working under the broad direction of the Associate Director, Careers & Employability, this role plays a vital part in supporting students to make informed career decisions, develop career management skills, and successfully transition into employment. Key Responsibilities: Provide one-on-one career coaching and guidance to students Support career planning, decision-making, job search strategies, and employability development. Design, develop, facilitate and evaluate career development programs, workshops, webinars, and presentations. Create, review and maintain career development resources, online content, publications, and digital learning materials. Build and maintain strong relationships with employers, industry partners, and university stakeholders to support student career outcomes. Promote Careers & Employability services across the university community. Represent the university at industry events, employer engagement activities, and relevant internal committees. About you: Relevant experience and/or qualifications in career development, career coaching, or career advisory services. Membership with the Career Development Association of Australia (CDAA) or the National Association of Graduate Careers Advisory Services (NAGCAS) will be highly regarded Excellent communication and presentation skills, with the ability to effectively engage and present to diverse audiences. Ability to develop, review, and deliver career development content and programs, both online and in person. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be explored on our “ Work at UC ” site which includes: Flexible working arrangements Family-friendly policies On campus Gym, Medical services, Cafes, Post office, Supermarket and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. Professional Development offerings (study assistance, corporate programs and discounts) Access to Employee Assistance Program and a corporate private Health Plan (Bupa) What we need from you: To be considered for this position, we require your CV and a cover letter explaining what skills you would bring to the role; no additional documents are necessary. Submit your CV through the “Apply Now” tab. We kindly ask that you take this opportunity to align your CV with the Position Description, ensuring that your skills and experience are clearly articulated in connection with the specific requirements of the role. Working rights: Applicants who wish to apply for this position must have valid working rights at the time of submission. WWVP: The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au For job specific information: please contact Yvonne Soper, Associate Director, Careers & Employability at Yvonne.Soper@canberra.edu.au For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 01 November 2026 Advertised: 16 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504848/lecturer-in-nursing": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Nursing",
      "description": "Lecturer in Nursing •Fantastic opportunity to shape the future of nursing education •Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super (Pro Rata) •Multiple Vacancies, Up to 12 Month Fixed Term, Part-time and Full-time Arrangement Job no: 504848 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Teaching and Research, Nursing and Midwifery Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description About us: At the University of Canberra, we’re a welcoming and connected academic community shaped by the people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. Our research focuses on real-world challenges, working alongside partners to create outcomes that matter, while our teaching builds confidence and capability for the future. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, UC is a place where you can grow ideas, contribute knowledge, and make a difference. About the role: UC is seeking several passionate Lecturers in Nursing to join the team to help develop the next generation of nursing professionals. This is an exciting opportunity to combine your clinical expertise with innovative teaching practices in a supportive and forward-thinking academic environment. Working closely with the Discipline Lead and academic colleagues, you will lead and coordinate nursing units, support student learning, and contribute to curriculum innovation and quality improvement initiatives. Multiple Vacancies, Up to 12 Month Fixed Term, Part-time and Full-time Arrangement On Offer Key responsibilities: Convene and deliver nursing units across a range of teaching modes Coordinate and supporting teaching teams Design, review and enhance curriculum, assessments and learning resources to support student success. Ensure a positive and engaging student experience Provide high-quality teaching, assessment and timely, constructive feedback to students Support student progression by providing academic guidance Build strong relationships with industry partners, clinical education stakeholders and professional networks About you: To be successful in this role, you will bring: AHPRA registration Current registration as a Registered Nurse with the Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia (NMBA) A master’s qualification in Nursing or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of qualifications and professional experience. Experience teaching and assessing nursing students in a higher education setting Experience coordinating units and working collaboratively with teaching teams and stakeholders. Completion of, or current enrolment in, a PhD in Nursing, Health or a related discipline (Highly Desirable) Flexible and collaborative team player with a down-to-earth approach, focused on finding practical, solutions-driven outcomes Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights at the time of submission. The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au How to apply: Please apply with you CV only, no other documentation is required at this stage. Please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. For job specific information: please contact Mary-Ellen Hooper - Discipline Lead in Nursing - Mary-Ellen.Hooper@canberra.edu.au - 02 62012108 For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 1 November 2026 Advertised: 15 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504849/lecturer-in-nursing": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Nursing",
      "description": "Lecturer in Nursing • Fantastic opportunity to shape the future of nursing education • Academic Level B, Salary Range $116,403pa - $137,865 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time, Continuing Opportunity Job no: 504849 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Nursing and Midwifery Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description About us: At the University of Canberra, we’re a welcoming and connected academic community shaped by the people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. Our research focuses on real-world challenges, working alongside partners to create outcomes that matter, while our teaching builds confidence and capability for the future. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, UC is a place where you can grow ideas, contribute knowledge, and make a difference. About the role: UC is seeking a passionate Lecturer in Nursing to join the team to help develop the next generation of nursing professionals. This is an exciting opportunity to combine your clinical expertise with innovative teaching practices in a supportive and forward-thinking academic environment. Working closely with the Discipline Lead and academic colleagues, you will lead and coordinate nursing units, support student learning, and contribute to curriculum innovation and quality improvement initiatives. Key responsibilities: Convene and deliver nursing units across a range of teaching modes Coordinate and supporting teaching teams Design, review and enhance curriculum, assessments and learning resources to support student success Ensure a positive and engaging student experience Provide high-quality teaching, assessment and timely, constructive feedback to students Support student progression by providing academic guidance Build strong relationships with industry partners, clinical education stakeholders and professional networks About you: To be successful in this role, you will bring: AHPRA registration Current registration as a Registered Nurse with the Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia (NMBA) A master’s qualification in Nursing or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of qualifications and professional experience Experience teaching and assessing nursing students in a higher education setting Experience coordinating units and working collaboratively with teaching teams and stakeholders Completion of, or current enrolment in, a PhD in Nursing, Health or a related discipline (Highly Desirable) Flexible and collaborative team player with a down-to-earth approach, focused on finding practical, solutions-driven outcomes Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights at the time of submission. The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au How to apply: Please apply with you CV only, no other documentation is required at this stage. Please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. For job specific information: please contact Mary-Ellen Hooper - Discipline Lead in Nursing - Mary-Ellen.Hooper@canberra.edu.au - 02 62012108 For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 1 November 2026 Advertised: 15 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504847/clinical-educator-occupational-therapy": {
      "title": "Clinical Educator - Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Clinical Educator - Occupational Therapy • Shaping the next generation of occupational therapists • UC Level 8, Salary Range $116,009 pa - $129,394 pa plus 17% Super (pro rata) • Part-time (0.7 FTE - 24.5 hrs/ week), Two Year Fixed Term Opportunity Job no: 504847 Work type: Professional Location: Bruce Categories: Student Support Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description About us: University of Canberra is more than a university, it’s a community committed to shaping a better world through education, research, and opportunity with a strong commitment to inclusivity and reducing inequalities. Our vibrant campus in Australia’s capital city is a hub of innovation & opportunity. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate outcomes and student support, UC values progress over perfection, inclusion over competition, and real‑world impact over prestige. If you’re looking for a career that matters, where you can belong, grow, and help shape what’s next, you’ll find your place at UC. About the opportunity: The UC Health Clinics is seeking an experienced and passionate Occupational Therapy Clinical Educator. Reporting to the UC Health Clinics Clinical Convenor, the Clinical Educator will develop, implement, and oversee student-led occupational therapy services aligned with academic learning outcomes, research opportunities, and community needs. This is a fixed term position for 24 months, at 0.7 FTE (24.5 hours per week). Key Responsibilities: Provide high-quality, evidence-based clinical education and supervision to occupational therapy students undertaking placements within the UC Health Clinics. Coordinate student placement activities, including clinic timetabling and management of client caseloads. Collaborate with the Discipline Lead, Clinical Placement Coordinator, and academic staff to enhance student learning experiences and ensure strong alignment with curriculum outcomes. Support the development and delivery of innovative student-led occupational therapy services. Build and maintain relationships with community organisations, healthcare providers, and stakeholders to identify opportunities for service delivery and student learning. Maintain continuity of client care through provision of follow-up treatment and clinical services during periods when students are unavailable. Facilitate placement opportunities for students from external universities when appropriate. Work closely with the Clinical Convenor and Practice Manager to oversee clinical records, patient databases, and research data, ensuring compliance with privacy and confidentiality requirements. About you: To be considered for this position, you will have: Current registration as an Occupational Therapist with AHPRA. Demonstrated clinical experience in occupational therapy practice. Experience supervising, mentoring, or educating students and/or early-career clinicians. Strong understanding of evidence-based practice and contemporary occupational therapy service delivery. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build effective relationships across academic, clinical, and community settings. Commitment to high-quality client care and positive student learning outcomes. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be explored on our “ Work at UC ” site which includes: Flexible working arrangements Family-friendly policies On campus Gym, Medical services, Cafes, Post office, Supermarket and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. Professional Development offerings (study assistance, corporate programs and discounts) Access to Employee Assistance Program and a corporate private Health Plan (Bupa) How to apply: To be considered for this position, please “apply” with your Resume; no additional documents are necessary at this stage. We kindly ask that you take this opportunity to align your Resume with the Position Description , ensuring that your skills and experience are clearly articulated in connection with the specific requirements of the role. Working rights: Applicants who wish to apply for this position must have valid working rights at the time of submission. WWVP: The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au For job specific information: please contact Allyson Flynn - Clinical Convenor - UC Health Clinics - Allyson.Flynn@canberra.edu.au - 02 6201 5843 . For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 01 November 2026 Advertised: 13 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504958/associate-dean-indigenous-sh": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, Indigenous (S&H)",
      "description": "Associate Dean, Indigenous (S&H) • Lead Indigenous Excellence. Shape Research. Transform Futures. • Academic Level E or D, Salary Range $170,522 pa - $218,799 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time, Continuing Opportunity (Part-time options considered) Job no: 504958 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Teaching and Research Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Associate Dean Indigenous (Faculty of Science & Health) Lead Indigenous Excellence. Shape Research. Transform Futures. Academic Level E or D, Salary Range $170,522 pa - $218,799 pa plus 17% Super Full Time, Continuing Opportunity (Part-time options considered) About us: At the University of Canberra, we’re a welcoming and connected academic community shaped by the people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. Our research focuses on real-world challenges, working alongside partners to create outcomes that matter, while our teaching builds confidence and capability for the future. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, UC is a place where you can grow ideas, contribute knowledge, and make a difference. About the Faculty The Faculty of Science & Health is a dynamic and research-intensive academic community dedicated to improving health, wellbeing and quality of life through excellence in teaching, research, innovation and engagement. Bringing together expertise across nursing, midwifery, rehabilitation, sport and exercise science, behavioural and human sciences, public health, psychology, social work, disability, biomedical science, environmental science and applied health sciences, the Faculty fosters a highly collaborative and interdisciplinary environment where researchers, educators and industry partners work together to address some of society's most pressing health, environmental and social challenges. The Faculty is recognised for research excellence, innovative education and strong industry partnerships that translate evidence into meaningful social impact. It provides an outstanding environment for academic leadership, interdisciplinary collaboration and research growth, supporting nationally and internationally significant research across health and scientific disciplines. About the role: The Faculty is seeking an academic with a recognised research track record and a demonstrated commitment to Indigenous research excellence. This is a significant academic leadership opportunity for an accomplished researcher and educator who is passionate about advancing Indigenous excellence, strengthening Indigenous research capability, and driving meaningful institutional transformation. Reporting to the Dean, the Associate Dean Indigenous (ADI) will provide strategic leadership to advance Indigenous excellence, student success, research growth and community engagement across the Faculty. Working closely with the Pro Vice-Chancellor Indigenous and senior University leaders, the Associate Dean Indigenous will drive implementation of Indigenous strategic priorities while maintaining an active academic profile. Key responsibilities: Lead and influence Indigenous research strategy and capability development across the Faculty. Maintain a strong and active research profile with high-quality publications, scholarly outputs and academic recognition Supervise and mentor Higher Degree by Research (HDR) candidates, with a particular focus on supporting Indigenous research students and emerging scholars. Foster interdisciplinary and community-led research partnerships that create meaningful outcomes for Indigenous peoples and communities. Develop and strengthen research collaborations across academia, industry, government and community sectors. Support the growth of competitive research funding opportunities and strategic research initiatives. About you: A PhD in a relevant discipline. An established research profile with a publication records commensurate with appointment as Associate Professor or Professor. Demonstrated success in HDR supervision and research mentorship. Significant academic leadership experience across Indigenous learning and teaching, research, engagement and/or strategic initiatives. A strong understanding of contemporary Indigenous issues within higher education and the broader national context. A demonstrated commitment to Indigenous student success, Indigenous staff development and Indigenous research excellence. Previous experience as an Associate Dean Indigenous or in a comparable senior Indigenous leadership role will be advantageous. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Identification as an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person. The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au How to apply: Please apply with you CV and a cover letter outlining your interest and suitability. Also, please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. For job specific information: please contact Rachel Gibson, Executive Dean - DeanofHealth@canberra.edu.au For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 22 November 2026 Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504957/associate-dean-indigenous-dts": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, Indigenous (DT&S)",
      "description": "Associate Dean, Indigenous (DT&S) • Lead Indigenous Excellence. Shape Research. Transform Futures. • Academic Level E or D, Salary Range $170,522 pa - $218,799 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time, Continuing Opportunity (Part-time options considered) Job no: 504957 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Teaching and Research Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Associate Dean Indigenous (Faculty of Design, Technology & Society) Lead Indigenous Excellence. Shape Research. Transform Futures. Academic Level E or D, Salary Range $170,522 pa - $218,799 pa plus 17% Super Full Time, Continuing Opportunity (Part-time options considered) About us: At the University of Canberra, we’re a welcoming and connected academic community shaped by the people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. Our research focuses on real-world challenges, working alongside partners to create outcomes that matter, while our teaching builds confidence and capability for the future. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, UC is a place where you can grow ideas, contribute knowledge, and make a difference. About the Faculty The Faculty of Design, Technology & Society is a future-focused and multidisciplinary academic community committed to creating positive societal impact through excellence in education, research, innovation and engagement. Bringing together expertise across the humanities, education, creative industries, professional disciplines, design, the built environment and digital technologies, the Faculty provides a vibrant and collaborative environment where creativity, critical inquiry and technological innovation intersect. Through collaboration across disciplines and partnerships with external stakeholders, the Faculty creates opportunities for innovation, applied research and real-world impact. About the role: The Faculty is seeking an academic with a recognised research track record and a demonstrated commitment to Indigenous research excellence. This is a newly created role in our recent faculty amalgamation and a significant academic leadership opportunity for an accomplished researcher and educator who is passionate about advancing Indigenous excellence, strengthening Indigenous research capability, and driving meaningful institutional advocacy. Reporting to the Executive Dean, the Associate Dean Indigenous (ADI) will provide strategic leadership to advance Indigenous excellence, student success, research growth and community engagement across the faculty. Also working closely with the Pro Vice-Chancellor Indigenous and senior university leaders, the ADI will drive implementation of Indigenous strategic priorities while maintaining an active academic profile through research, supervision and scholarly leadership. This role will be critical in advancing the University's strategic priorities through industry partnerships, work-integrated learning, international engagement, Indigenous leadership and community collaboration. Key responsibilities: Lead and influence Indigenous research strategy and capability development across the Faculty. Maintain a strong and active academic research profile Supervise HDR candidates, with a focus on supporting Indigenous research students Foster interdisciplinary and community-led research partnerships that create meaningful outcomes for Indigenous peoples and communities. Develop and strengthen research collaborations across academia, industry, government and community sectors. Support the growth of competitive research funding opportunities and strategic research initiatives. About you: A PhD in a relevant discipline within the faculty profile. An established research profile with a publication records commensurate with appointment as Associate Professor or Professor. Demonstrated success in HDR supervision and research mentorship. Significant academic leadership experience across Indigenous learning and teaching, research, engagement and/or strategic initiatives. A strong understanding of contemporary Indigenous issues within higher education and the broader national context. A demonstrated commitment to Indigenous student success, Indigenous staff development and Indigenous research excellence. Previous experience as an Associate Dean Indigenous or in a comparable senior Indigenous leadership role will be advantageous Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Identification as an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person. The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au How to apply: Please apply with you CV and a cover letter outlining your interest and suitability. Also, please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for. For job specific information: please contact Julian Knowles, Executive Dean - DeanofFAD@canberra.edu.au For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 22 November 2026 Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504869/ssaf-and-funding-programs-coordinator": {
      "title": "SSAF and Funding Programs Coordinator",
      "description": "SSAF and Funding Programs Coordinator • Key role in supporting the University's key student services and funding programs • UC Level 6, Salary Range $93,705 pa - $100,871 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time, Two-Year Fixed Term Job no: 504869 Work type: Professional Location: Bruce Categories: Administration, Project Management Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description About us: University of Canberra is more than a university, it’s a community committed to shaping a better world through education, research, and opportunity with a strong commitment to inclusivity and reducing inequalities. Our vibrant campus in Australia’s capital city is a hub of innovation & opportunity. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate outcomes and student support, UC values progress over perfection, inclusion over competition, and real‑world impact over prestige. If you’re looking for a career that matters, where you can belong, grow, and help shape what’s next, you’ll find your place at UC. About the role: This is an exciting opportunity to play a key role in supporting the University's funding, planning and accountability functions. As the SSAF and Funding Programs Coordinator, you will lead the coordination and administration of the University's Student Services and Amenities Fee (SSAF) program and provide support for other funding and grant programs managed through the Planning & Assurance team. Working across a diverse range of stakeholders including Finance, Governance, student representative bodies and senior University leaders, you will help ensure funding programs are administered transparently, effectively and in compliance with legislative and reporting requirements. You will also contribute to the implementation of the University's future student-led SSAF allocation model and help enhance funding administration processes across the institution. Please note this is a Full Time, Two-Year Fixed Term position. Key Responsibilities: Coordinate the annual SSAF funding cycle, including consultation, application processes, allocations, acquittals and reporting. Support the implementation and ongoing administration of the University's student-led SSAF allocation arrangements. Work closely with Finance to support revenue forecasting, funding allocation planning and ongoing monitoring. Maintain accurate records and reporting systems to support transparency, audit readiness and governance obligations. Assist with administration of other internal or external funding programs, grants or strategic funding sources managed through Planning & Assurance. About you: Experience managing financial information, budgets, acquittals, funding records or related administrative processes. Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities, deadlines and competing stakeholder requirements. Experience preparing reports, briefing papers, correspondence and administrative documentation. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with a diverse range of stakeholders. Strong attention to detail and commitment to governance, compliance and record-keeping standards. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits such as: Flexible working arrangements Family-friendly policies On campus Gym, Medical services, Cafes, Post office, Supermarket and Childcare facilities. Professional Development offerings (study assistance, corporate programs and discounts) Innovative work environment with a diverse and inclusive culture Access to Employee Assistance Program and a corporate private Health Plan (Bupa) How to apply: To be considered for this position, we require your Resume and a One-Page cover letter explaining what skills you would bring to the role and how you meet the role requirements; no additional documents are necessary. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. Working rights: Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights at the time of submission. For job specific information: please contact Simon Wheeler, Manager, Grant Accounting Services, Simon.Wheeler@canberra.edu.au For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 08 November 2026 Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504882/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Fellow • Join UC’s world-leading Centre for Deliberative Democracy (CDD) as a Postdoctoral Research Fellow contributing to an Australian Research Council (ARC) Discovery Project. • UC Level B, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $137,865 pa + 17% Super • Full Time, research-focused, 2-year fixed term, based in Canberra, Australia Job no: 504882 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Research Only Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description About us: University of Canberra’s vision is that “Together we work to empower, connect and share knowledge with our people, cultures and places.” UC is engrained in the local community and we aim to challenge the status quo through the pursuit of excellence in teaching, learning and research. The University of Canberra has been ranked in the top 7 universities in the world for reducing inequalities (THE Impact Rankings 2024). About the role: Join the world-leading Centre for Deliberative Democracy (CDD) as a Postdoctoral Fellow on a nationally significant research project exploring how major international conflicts shape public debate, social cohesion and democratic life in Australia. We are seeking an outstanding Postdoctoral Fellow to join the CDD within the Faculty of Business, Government and Law. This research-focused position is funded through the Australian Research Council Discovery Project, Foreign Conflicts, Domestic Divides: Advancing a Deliberative Response , led by Professor Selen Ercan, Emeritus Distinguished Professor John Dryzek and Dr Jordan McSwiney, along with project partners across other Australian universities. The project brings research on intractable conflicts into conversation with deliberative democratic theory and public sphere research. Empirically, it examines how the Isreal-Palestine and Russia-Ukraine conflicts spill over into the Australian public sphere, focusing on the communicative dynamics through which these conflicts are reproduced, contested or transformed. Combining normative democratic theory with large-scale computational analysis and in-depth qualitative research, the project aims to develop a deliberative approach to understanding and responding to intractable conflicts. Key Responsibilities Contribute to the development of a deliberative theoretical framework for understanding and responding to intractable conflicts and their domestic spillover effects. Conduct empirical research (drawing on qualitative and/or mixed-methods, fieldwork) to examine how foreign conflicts influence communication dynamics across parliamentary, media, digital, civil society and everyday public sphere settings. Connect empirical findings to broader normative questions in the field of deliberative democracy concerning disagreement, polarisation, mutual understanding, deliberation and democratic legitimacy. Lead and contribute to publications in high-quality national and international journals. Organise research workshops, conference panels and scholarly events. Participate actively in the intellectual life of the Centre for Deliberative Democracy About you: You are an ambitious and self-directed researcher with passion in deliberative democracy and a strong publication record, currently holding PhD in Political Science, Sociology, Media and Communication, or closely aligned discipline, or completed before the time of commencement of the position. You must be able to live and work in Australia if successful for this role. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be explored on our “ Work at UC ” site which includes: Flexible working arrangements Family-friendly policies On campus Gym, Medical services, Cafes, Post office, Supermarket and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. Professional Development offerings (study assistance, corporate programs and discounts) Access to Employee Assistance Program and a corporate private Health Plan (Bupa) University of Canberra is a values based organisation and sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via Connected – A Decadal Strategy 2023-2032 . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Applications are invited from both domestic and international candidates. Applicants must be eligible to live and work in Australia for the duration of the appointment and must reside in Canberra throughout the fellowship. Submit your Application through the “Apply Now” tab. As part of your application please submit: an academic CV, including the names and contact details of two referees; a one-page cover letter outlining your suitability for the position with reference to the primary responsibilities; and one writing sample (a published or unpublished journal article or thesis chapter) demonstrating expertise in deliberative democratic theory and qualitative empirical research. For job specific information: Jordan McSwiney, Senior Research Fellow, Centre for Deliberative Democracy, jordan.mcswiney@canberra.edu.au. For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . If you would like to request a reasonable adjustment to the selection process, please feel free to contact us. Closing date: 11.55pm, Wednesday 18 November 2026 Advertised: 19 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504900/clinical-liaison-nurse": {
      "title": "Clinical Liaison Nurse",
      "description": "Clinical Liaison Nurse • Empower nursing students to thrive in real clinical settings • UC Level 8, Salary Range $116,009 pa - $129,394 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time Continuing Opportunity Job no: 504900 Work type: Professional Location: Bruce Categories: Medical and Counselling, Student Support Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description About us: University of Canberra is more than a university, it’s a community committed to shaping a better world through education, research, and opportunity with a strong commitment to inclusivity and reducing inequalities. Our vibrant campus in Australia’s capital city is a hub of innovation, opportunity and a launchpad for a diverse cohort including first-in-family students and future leaders alike. If you are looking for a career that matters with a welcoming, values based, forward-thinking institution, come build your future with us. About the role: As a Clinical Liaison Nurse, you will play a pivotal role in supporting Bachelor and Master of Nursing students during their Professional Experience Placement (PEP). Acting as the key link between students, clinical settings, and the University of Canberra, you will help shape meaningful placement experiences while strengthening partnerships across the healthcare sector. Key responsibilities: Facilitate and support nursing students undertaking PEP in a variety of health care facilities, settings and specialties on rotating rosters. Build and maintain strong relationships with industry stakeholders, including clinical leaders and nursing staff. Monitor student progress, provide timely feedback, and support those requiring additional development. Facilitate high-quality placement experiences that align with both university and industry expectations. About you: You are an experienced and compassionate AHPRA Registered Nurse who brings strong clinical insight, excellent communication skills, and a genuine passion for supporting student learning in real-world settings. To be successful, you will have: Demonstrated experience as a Registered Nurse and recent clinical experience in general Nursing settings Completed or working towards a postgraduate qualification in Nursing Demonstrated experience in delivering education and facilitating group learning initiatives Strong stakeholder engagement and communication skills, and confidence using digital systems and administrative tools The ability to manage diverse situations with professionalism, discretion, and empathy Please note: This role requires regular travel to various locations across Canberra. A current driver's licence and access to a reliable vehicle are essential. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be explored on our “ Work at UC ” site which includes: Flexible working arrangements Family-friendly policies On campus Gym, Medical services, Cafes, Post office, Supermarket and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. Professional Development offerings (study assistance, corporate programs and discounts) Access to Employee Assistance Program and a corporate private Health Plan (Bupa) How to apply: Please submit your CV and a 1-page cover letter outlining your experience in clinical practice and/or nursing education, and how this has prepared you to support student learning in clinical settings. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview/written assessment. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. Working rights: Applicants who wish to apply for this position must have valid working rights at the time of submission. WWVP: The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au For job specific information: please contact Mx Heath Hind, Lecturer, School of Nursing & Midwifery, Heath.Hind@canberra.edu.au . For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . If you would like to request a reasonable adjustment to the selection process, please feel free to contact us. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 01 Nov 2026 Advertised: 19 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://uctalent.canberra.edu.au/cw/en/job/504884/lecturer-in-environmental-science": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Environmental Science",
      "description": "Lecturer in Environmental Science • Fantastic opportunity to shape the future of Environmental Science education • Academic Level B or C (based on experience), Salary Range $116,403pa - $159,162 pa plus 17% Super • Full Time, Continuing Opportunity Job no: 504884 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Education Focused, Science - Environmental Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description About us: At the University of Canberra, we’re a welcoming and connected academic community shaped by the people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. Our research focuses on real-world challenges, working alongside partners to create outcomes that matter, while our teaching builds confidence and capability for the future. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, UC is a place where you can grow ideas, contribute knowledge, and make a difference. About the Faculty The Faculty of Science & Health is a dynamic and research-intensive academic community dedicated to improving health, wellbeing and quality of life through excellence in teaching, research, innovation and engagement. Bringing together expertise across nursing, midwifery, rehabilitation, sport and exercise science, behavioural and human sciences, public health, psychology, social work, disability, biomedical science, environmental science and applied health sciences, the Faculty fosters a highly collaborative and interdisciplinary environment where researchers, educators and industry partners work together to address some of society's most pressing health, environmental and social challenges. About the role: We are seeking an enthusiastic and collaborative academic to join our Environmental Science team as a Lecturer in Environmental Science. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to a growing and research-active discipline while helping to educate the next generation of environmental professionals. As a Lecturer, you will play a key role in delivering outstanding teaching, building a successful research profile, supervising student research projects, and engaging with industry, government and community partners. Your work will contribute to the University's commitment to addressing contemporary environmental challenges and strengthening our research impact. Please note: For this role, we are open to consider suitable candidates at either Lecturer (Academic Level B) or Senior Lecturer level (Academic Level C). Key responsibilities: Teach and coordinate undergraduate and postgraduate units in Environmental Science and related disciplines. Deliver engaging and inclusive learning experiences across face-to-face, blended and online settings. Design, review and enhance curriculum, assessment and learning resources to support student success and graduate employability. Develop and grow a research program aligned with the University's environmental research strengths. Publish high-quality research outputs and seek competitive research funding. Supervise undergraduate research projects, Honours students and HDR candidates. Maintain high standards of research integrity, ethics, safety and professional practice. About you: To be successful in this role, you will bring: A completed doctoral qualification in Applied Environmental Science or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated ability to teach and convene relevant units effectively across face-to-face, blended and online modes. Demonstrated capacity to supervise undergraduate projects, Honours students, and HDR candidates effectively. Expertise in an area aligned with the current research strengths in Applied Environmental Science: freshwater ecology, ecosystem processes, conservation ecology, genomics, or related fields A developing or established track record of high-quality research publications. Excellent communication, organisational and interpersonal skills. A commitment to inclusion, diversity, cultural safety and student-centred learning. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights at the time of submission. The University of Canberra is committed to the safety of vulnerable and young people. As such, successful applicants will be required to have a current ACT working with vulnerable people registration. For further details on how to apply please click https://www.accesscanberra.act.gov.au How to apply: Please apply with you CV and a one-page cover letter outlining your interest and suitability. Also, please ensure you take the time to align your CV with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to the position you are applying for If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete an online one-way video interview. There will be a list of pre-set questions that will need to be answered within a stipulated time. For job specific information: please contact Claire O'Brien- Head of School, Science - claire.obrien@canberra.edu.au For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Wednesday 11 November 2026 Advertised: 28 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
